WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.600
OK, so right now we have
the indicators here,

00:07.200 --> 00:09.400
based on the sensors
we have over here,

00:09.700 --> 00:12.100
and the health prediction
is already running.

00:12.600 --> 00:16.600
It comes from the neural network,
which was first calibrated

00:17.000 --> 00:22.100
with the initial parameters and normalized,
so that, for example, here,

00:22.600 --> 00:27.500
if we start blocking
the fan's airflow,

00:27.800 --> 00:32.800
the current draw then starts
to rise on the dashboard,

00:33.400 --> 00:36.900
and the health score
also starts to drop.

00:37.300 --> 00:39.000
So we have three states:

00:39.800 --> 00:41.100
maintenance required,

00:41.800 --> 00:46.100
then we also have
the warning state,

00:47.300 --> 00:50.300
and then the
no-maintenance-needed state.

00:50.300 --> 00:54.300
It changes with current,
temperature, and vibration.

00:54.700 --> 00:59.000
For example, if we hit the table,
it detects more vibration.

00:59.000 --> 01:02.600
You can see it going up.

01:03.400 --> 01:05.700
And here it explains the cause

01:06.400 --> 01:08.600
of the maintenance warning,
and it also shows

01:09.800 --> 01:11.600
how the parameters
are detected.

01:12.000 --> 01:14.000
In this case,
it shows how the value rises

01:14.900 --> 01:17.200
and how that shows up
in the health score.
